ook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHNO, NAOTO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOPPAN PRINTING CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, EIZABURO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKIMOTO YASUMASA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI JUNICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO ISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MINATO TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA RYUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA IKUMA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHIRA KATSUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHNO NAOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE EIZABURO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKIMOTO, YASUMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, JUNICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, ISAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MINATO, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, IKUMA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHIRA, KATSUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHNO, NAOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, EIZABURO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A production method for a plasma display panel comprising the steps of forming on and filling in a partition-forming recessed board a paste layer with a constant thickness using a paste-like partition-forming material containing glass frits, placing the paste-like partition-forming material-filled partition-forming recessed board on a substrate and transferring the paste-like partition-forming material onto the substrate, and heating the paste-like partition-forming material to burn away organic components and at the same time sinter the glass frits, thereby forming a partition and a dielectric layer. A plasma display panel produced by this method has its partition wall and dielectric layer formed from the same, paste-like partition-forming material containing low-melting-point glass frits.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un procédé de production d'un écran à plasma consistant à former une couche de pâte d'une épaisseur constante sur une plaque à évidements formant des cloisons, en utilisant un matériau pâteux susceptible de former des cloisons et contenant de la fritte de verre; à placer la plaque à évidements formant des cloisons, remplie du matériau pâteux susceptible de former des cloisons sur un substrat et à transférer le matériau pâteux susceptible de former des cloisons sur ledit substrat, puis à chauffer ce matériau de manière à brûler les composants organiques et en même temps à agglomérer par frittage la fritte de verre, de manière à former une cloison et une couche diélectrique. L'invention se rapporte à un écran à plasma produit selon ledit procédé, qui comporte sa paroi de cloisonnement et sa couche diélectrique formées dans le même matériau pâteux susceptible de former des cloisons qui contient la fritte de verre à faible point de fusion.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>